00:14:21.530 --> 00:14:22.890
It's TensorFlow.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:24.080
And how is it based on--

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.040
RAM RAMANATHAN: Yeah.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:28.216
Could you explain what's the
relationship between TensorFlow

00:14:28.216 --> 00:14:29.660
on Google- not Google Photos.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.985
Google Cloud Vision API?

00:14:30.985 --> 00:14:31.860
RAM RAMANATHAN: Sure.

00:14:35.946 --> 00:14:40.520
One of the things is the way all
these machine learning models

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.754
evolved the recent future
to enable and allow

00:14:42.754 --> 00:14:44.170
these powerful
scenarios is really

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:45.651
advances in deep learning.

00:14:45.651 --> 00:14:46.150
Right?

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.608
So deep learning
enables you really

00:14:47.608 --> 00:14:51.680
look at unstructured data,
whether it's images, videos,

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:56.160
and really start identifying
patterns in your data set

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.580
And within Google,
we have been using

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.240
a framework called TensorFlow
to drive a lot of the scenarios.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:05.200
And we recently open
sourced that in November.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.720
And we had great reception.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.580
A lot of great user adoption.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:11.160
And so internally
at Google we've

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.220
been leveraging frameworks like
that, to build these models.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.030
And what we have done
on the Vision API

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:20.290
is basically just providing
wrappers around that for users

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:20.880
to consume it.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:23.450
So you can imagine that people
use deep learning frameworks

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.430
to build these
sophisticated models,

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:27.630
and then basically once
the models are ready to go,

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.710
we're exposing
that as REST APIs.

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:31.795
MARK MANDEL: That's very cool.

00:15:31.795 --> 00:15:34.211
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Also, could
you give us a little bit more

00:15:34.211 --> 00:15:38.960
