use TensorFlow at Google?

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.020
RAM RAMANATHAN: Yep.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:44.630
Inside Google, we're using
TensorFlow from everything

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:49.610
from speech recognition in
the Google app, in OK Google,

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.426
to how we do things around
smart reply and inboxes--

00:15:52.426 --> 00:15:53.300
that's a new feature.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.850
We just introduced an inbox
that allows you to intelligently

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:02.420
pick common responses to your
emails coming into your inbox--

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:05.400
to how we do image
searches in Google Photos.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.570
One of the interesting
things about TensorFlow

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:11.980
is its ability to adapt to
a broad set of scenarios.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:13.810
And also the fact
that its ability

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:17.216
to run not just on
a single smartphone,

00:16:17.216 --> 00:16:19.340
but across thousands of
computers and data centers.

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.490
So its ability to
scale, where you can now

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:25.870
imagine some of these models
running on your Android device

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:27.485
or Google box.

00:16:27.485 --> 00:16:29.360
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Something
